PSI-RING

This is a version 1.06 of a ringing program for the Psion Series 3 pocket computer. It is written in OPL, the BASIC-like programming language built into the machine.

Improvements over the beta test version include: many bugs removed; ability to display lines right to left for those tied to Snowden-type diagrams (default); increased on-line help.

Ver 1.06: better sync of sound in simulator; configuration of file paths for methods, help and icon files.

The program is to help beginners and improvers in change-ringing and so has several limitations, especially a maximum of 8 bells and about 300 changes. A fully-fledged simulator it is not!

The main functions are:

(1)	Method display: table of numbers, single lead with bell paths; blue-line.

(2)	Transposition: shows lead heads after calls

(3)	Simulator: you can prove you do(n't) know the method by ringing one bell while the computer provides ?perfect striking on the others.

Methods are held in psion database format and can be entered or edited (in place notation) using the psion database tool.

This version is distributed as a test version by Adam Green,. Email: Compuserve 100064,2776 (or >INTERNET:10064,2776@compuserve.com.

I would appreciate any reports of bugs and other unexpected 'features', plus suggestions for improvements. Actually, just knowing someone out there is also using a Psion 3 for this purpose would be an encouragement!
 
The files that should form part of this package are:

	Ring.opa = main program to be installed in the System window. Store in APPS directory

	Methods.dbf = methods library - a standard Psion database file which can be modified using the database tool. Store in same APP directory and drive as Psiring.opa.

	Ringhelp.dbf = file of longer help messages called by key from the program (other messages are written into the source code).

NOTE: ringhelp and methods files must be closd before the psiring application is run. Conversely, you may get a 'file open error' if you try to update the dbf files while psiring is running. If this happens use Psion-X to quit Psiring and try again.

	Psiring.doc = this file.

	Method.doc = instructions for entering new methods.

Limitations
I have not yet mastered all the subtleties of OPAs and so it cannot be deleted from the System menu. Re-enter the program and use Psion-X to exit properly.
Error handling is limited so you are likely to crash out if you do something I have not thought of.
Your reports of problems will be most helpful.
